%N A398938 Decimal expansion of the volume of a canonical (dual-uniform) 10-gonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398938 The 10-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 10-gonal antiprism.
%H A398938 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398938/b398938.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 3..10000</a>
%H A398938 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Decagonal_antitegum">Decagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398938 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398938 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_08">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 8</a>.
%F A398938 Equals (10*(1 + 2*A019881)*A019979*csc(Pi/20)^2)/(12*sqrt(8*(1 + A019881))).
%F A398938 Equals the largest root of 6561*x^8 - 163806300*x^6 + 3846436875*x^4 - 156375000*x^2 + 390625.
%e A398938 157.9340462376767060140719983253458200950899015452...
%t A398938 First[RealDigits[Root[6561*#^8 - 163806300*#^6 + 3846436875*#^4 - 156375000*#^2 + 390625 &, 8], 10, 100]]
%t A398938 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398938 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 10}, "Volume"], 10, 100]]
%Y A398938 Cf. A398939 (surface area), A398940 (inradius), A398941 (midradius), A398942 (height).
%Y A398938 Cf. A398943 (long edge).
%Y A398938 Cf. A398944 (small face angle), A398945 (large face angle), A398946 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398938 Cf. A395804 (volume of the dual).
%Y A398938 Cf. A019881, A019979.
